# actives_rdrp.smi — known viral-polymerase nucleos(t)ide-analog inhibitors (SPEC #5).
# The ACTIVE set for the retrospective enrichment benchmark: nucleos(t)ide analogs that
# act at a viral RdRp / polymerase NTP site — the chemotype the 8PSO NTP pocket selects.
# SMILES are the canonical ChEMBL structures already committed in ligands_chembl.json
# (so every entry is real and reproducible). Format: `SMILES  name  CHEMBL_id`.
#
# Favipiravir is a known RdRp active but absent from the committed ChEMBL cache; resolve
# it via vta.data.ligands / pubchem seams when extending the set online.
CCC(CC)COC(=O)[C@H](C)N[P@](=O)(OC[C@H]1O[C@@](C#N)(c2ccc3c(N)ncnn23)[C@H](O)[C@@H]1O)Oc1ccccc1	Remdesivir	CHEMBL4065616
NC(=O)c1ncn([C@@H]2O[C@H](CO)[C@@H](O)[C@H]2O)n1	Ribavirin	CHEMBL1643
CC(C)OC(=O)[C@H](C)N[P@](=O)(OC[C@H]1O[C@@H](n2ccc(=O)[nH]c2=O)[C@](C)(F)[C@@H]1O)Oc1ccccc1	Sofosbuvir	CHEMBL1259059
CC(C)C(=O)OC[C@H]1O[C@@H](n2cc/c(=N\O)/[nH]c2=O)[C@H](O)[C@@H]1O	Molnupiravir	CHEMBL4650320
